[Testing] This block asserts nothing. The agent test harness exports **delta** temporality, so after `testing.clearData()` an unchanged measurement is exported as `0`. Since acquiring a bare semaphore permit changes neither `allConnections` nor `freeConnections` (as the comment itself says), `assertUsageMetric(pool, 0, 0, pool, 0, 0)` passes for *any* pool state — including an implementation that hardcodes `0`. Same for `pending_requests`, which is only ever asserted as `0`.

So `usedConnections` (`allConnections - freeConnections`) and `semaphore.queueSize()` currently have no coverage at all.

Suggestion below drives both: check a connection out of the holder (idle → used), then exhaust the pool's permits and queue one more acquisition. Values are deltas, hence `-1`/`+1`.

```suggestion
      ConnectionsHolder<RedisConnection> holder = getMasterConnectionsHolder((Redisson) redisson);
      AsyncSemaphore semaphore = holder.getFreeConnectionsCounter();

      // the agent test exporter uses delta temporality, so after clearData() the exported values
      // are deltas relative to the previous export
      testing.clearData();
      RedisConnection connection = holder.acquireConnection(RedisCommands.PING).join();
      try {
        // checking out a connection moves it from idle to used
        assertUsageMetric(regularPool, -1, 1, subscriptionPool, 0, 0);
      } finally {
        holder.releaseConnection(connection);
        holder.releaseConnection();
      }

      testing.clearData();
      for (int i = 0; i < REGULAR_MAX; i++) {
        semaphore.acquire().join();
      }
      // no permits left, this acquisition is queued
      CompletableFuture<Void> queued = semaphore.acquire();
      try {
        assertPendingRequests(regularPool, 1, subscriptionPool, 0);
      } finally {
        for (int i = 0; i < REGULAR_MAX + 1; i++) {
          semaphore.release();
        }
      }
      queued.join();
```

I ran `test` and `testStableSemconv` for this module with these changes and both pass.

